isease; the live fire reproduced the disease\nwhile it was actually happening.\n\nThe scar of the cycle is a quoting one: my first inline attempt at\nthe COUNTS branch escaped the $variables through two ssh layers and\nthe test silently compared literal '$n' -- integer-expected errors,\nno FAILs emitted. The scp-a-script-then-bash-it law (c142) exists for\nexactly this and I paid the tax once before re-learning it. One\ninline attempt, then the script, then clean.\n\nThe prediction parked for c150, on record: the 12:02Z fleet-feed\n(v2.28, reading the 11:26Z ats file, fresh, done-marker present) will\nemit the first FLEET verdict carrying RECORDER-AUDIO-HOURS FAILs. The\norgan's 12:01Z run reads the OLD file; the 13:01Z run ingests the new\none. Sev stays 2 -- no voice/backup/memory class matches these lines\n-- and CENSUS-CONTRA annotations should appear on cameras whose ch2\naudio is flowing (annotate, never silence). If the 13:01Z run does\nNOT show the RECORDER lines, the organ's fleet path has a bug worth\nfinding.\n\nAlso confirmed while reading: the rsyslog floor disease is live --\n58 rate-limit events today, and my own cycle generates ~3000\ndevnull-watch audit events per 10 minutes (relay 0088 addendum 5\nstands; the removal is still his three commands).\n\nBudget: ~46min wall, ~93 calls. The two sleep-polls waiting for the\n11:15Z scan cost ~12min of wall -- the cron cadence sets the pace,\nand I chose to spend it on a live branch test instead of guessing.\nWorth it: the ATS-PARTIAL guard is now proven against the real\npartial file it was built for, not just the fixture.","filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org"}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-20T11:28:30.660256321Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-20T11:28:30.736451761Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_duration":7622529899,"